WEBVTT

00:23.720 --> 00:24.840
[liquid pouring]

00:32.440 --> 00:33.600
[Churchill grunts]

00:33.680 --> 00:34.680
[sniffles]

00:38.040 --> 00:39.160
[sniffs]

00:40.320 --> 00:42.840
You prefer Irish to Scotch.

00:44.000 --> 00:45.680
Yes, Mr Churchill.

00:49.560 --> 00:51.200
Irish over Scotch.

00:52.440 --> 00:54.680
Cigarettes over Havana cigars.

00:55.440 --> 00:57.920
And your mother
was probably born in a tent.

00:59.760 --> 01:01.360
Grandmother in a tent,

01:02.120 --> 01:04.160
me mother on a narrowboat.

01:05.000 --> 01:09.760
And always happy to give smart answers
to men born better than you.

01:10.760 --> 01:14.240
A man needs to prove he is better than me

01:14.320 --> 01:16.720
rather than show me his birth certificate.

01:16.800 --> 01:20.800
See, I don't have one,
so they mean very little to me.

01:21.640 --> 01:23.720
You speak beautifully in the House.

01:24.440 --> 01:25.440
Thank you.

01:25.520 --> 01:28.600
And believe not a word
of what you are saying.

01:29.760 --> 01:34.240
Conviction introduces emotion,
which is the enemy of oratory.

01:34.320 --> 01:36.280
You read Greek literature.

01:36.840 --> 01:38.360
I have trouble sleeping.

01:39.800 --> 01:40.640
[inhales deeply]

01:42.480 --> 01:45.600
Is there a reason for your visit,
Mr Churchill?

01:46.520 --> 01:49.280
You are forming an alliance
with a fascist.

01:50.440 --> 01:55.160
So, I made some inquiries
amongst the worst people in Whitehall.

01:55.240 --> 01:59.840
And I found out that you are not
forming an alliance with him at all.

02:00.680 --> 02:02.120
You are spying on him.

02:02.640 --> 02:03.800
Yes.

02:04.560 --> 02:05.680
Why?

02:08.880 --> 02:10.480
The honest answer is…

02:12.280 --> 02:13.800
I'm no longer sure.

02:13.880 --> 02:17.000
Do you dig your own garden, Mr Shelby?

02:19.160 --> 02:20.240
I have a gardener.

02:21.360 --> 02:24.400
In fact, I have three gardeners.

02:25.520 --> 02:32.080
Three generations of men with no ambition
who are happier than I will ever be.

02:32.640 --> 02:35.080
Well, if you ask them,

02:35.720 --> 02:39.080
they will tell you that there are
certain species of weed,

02:39.680 --> 02:44.800
no matter how much you tug at them,
poison them, they continue to grow back.

02:46.000 --> 02:48.560
In the end, the only solution

02:48.640 --> 02:52.240
is to plough up the top soil,
create a field of mud

02:52.320 --> 02:55.400
and blow up and burn the exposed taproots.

02:56.600 --> 02:59.240
That's what you and I did in France.

02:59.960 --> 03:03.000
But when I hear that man Mosley speak,

03:03.600 --> 03:08.440
I see the green shoots of another war
growing up around his feet.

03:09.800 --> 03:13.320
And you see exactly the same thing I do.

03:14.200 --> 03:15.920
That's why you oppose him.

03:17.640 --> 03:21.200
Yeah. Your mystery solved.

03:23.840 --> 03:25.320
What is your strategy?

03:27.160 --> 03:28.880
I won't burden you with it.

03:29.560 --> 03:31.600
You're going to break the law.

03:33.240 --> 03:34.120
[breathes deeply]

03:35.080 --> 03:36.360
I need to sleep.

03:37.280 --> 03:38.880
You said you don't sleep.

03:39.760 --> 03:41.520
I said I have trouble sleeping.

03:42.800 --> 03:44.000
As do I.

03:45.440 --> 03:46.760
As do I.

03:48.600 --> 03:49.920
Mr Shelby,

03:50.760 --> 03:54.120
I have no doubt
that there was once a time in Flanders

03:54.760 --> 03:58.000
when you were under the ground
and I was above it,

03:58.800 --> 04:01.000
both working to the same end.

04:02.560 --> 04:07.440
We are in the same exact situation,
here in Westminster.

04:09.480 --> 04:12.640
Do what you have to do, Mr Shelby.

04:15.560 --> 04:16.400
[grunts]

04:16.480 --> 04:19.080
And if you need anything, call me.

04:24.160 --> 04:26.959
There are some times, some nights,

04:29.000 --> 04:31.960
when I don't see the point
of carrying on with any of it.

04:32.680 --> 04:33.520
[Churchill] Hmm.

04:35.000 --> 04:36.840
That old dance routine.

04:38.400 --> 04:43.360
I put out a cigar,
and an hour later, I want another.

04:44.800 --> 04:48.920
Sometimes, the bridge between hours
is as fragile as that.

04:50.200 --> 04:51.720
But use it anyway.

04:54.880 --> 05:01.000
A tent, then a boat,
then a house, now a mansion.

05:02.560 --> 05:04.920
That's something, isn't it?

05:06.720 --> 05:09.520
[sighs] Yeah, that is something.

05:13.760 --> 05:14.800
By the way,

05:16.080 --> 05:20.200
was it you who killed that
Ulsterman intelligence officer?

05:21.120 --> 05:22.400
I forget his name.

05:23.160 --> 05:25.160
-Major Campbell.
-Yes.

05:25.960 --> 05:27.880
-Campbell.
-No.

05:28.960 --> 05:30.200
It was me aunt.

05:31.160 --> 05:33.760
I really must come up
to Birmingham someday

05:33.840 --> 05:35.920
and spend an evening with your family.

05:36.920 --> 05:38.800
They sound interesting.

05:38.880 --> 05:41.360
Yes. We'd like that.

05:53.360 --> 05:54.320
[snorting]

05:58.520 --> 06:00.840
I got to Harold French refereeing
Liverpool for cash.

06:00.920 --> 06:02.680
Tom the tatter,
reffing Sheffield Wednesday,

06:02.760 --> 06:05.880
wants cash and a beating
for a bloke who's screwing his wife.

06:05.960 --> 06:08.200
Clap doctor said
go easy on the whiskey, yeah?

06:10.000 --> 06:11.040
Finn.

06:12.560 --> 06:13.880
You don't knock?

06:14.760 --> 06:15.800
No, Finn.

06:17.440 --> 06:18.600
I don't knock.

06:20.320 --> 06:21.400
All right.

06:23.280 --> 06:24.440
Hello, Billy.

06:26.040 --> 06:28.880
-How are you, mate?
-Good, Mr Shelby.

06:28.960 --> 06:30.440
[Arthur] Yeah, you look good.

06:32.240 --> 06:35.400
-That's a nice suit.
-[chuckles] Thank you, Mr Shelby.

06:35.480 --> 06:36.560
[Finn] He earned that suit.

06:36.640 --> 06:39.760
We made more on the matches
than we did on the races last Saturday.

06:39.840 --> 06:43.480
-He's a good man.
-Yeah, I know that. Mm.

06:44.040 --> 06:45.840
You're coming up in the world. I like it.

06:48.280 --> 06:50.080
How's the missus? Hmm?

06:51.160 --> 06:54.120
The old trouble and strife,
as the Cockneys like to call it.

06:54.200 --> 06:55.560
[Billy] She moved out.

06:55.640 --> 06:57.760
[Arthur] Oh. That's a shame.

06:58.400 --> 06:59.960
Why don't I join you, eh?

07:00.680 --> 07:04.720
Why don't I join the party?
Look at this. Having some fun. Hmm?

07:06.080 --> 07:06.960
[exhales heavily]

07:07.560 --> 07:08.960
You were a good man, Billy.

07:10.520 --> 07:12.360
You're a good man. Hmm?

07:13.560 --> 07:16.400
You could sing like a bird in a cage.

07:16.480 --> 07:18.640
[inhales sharply] What did we do, eh?

07:18.720 --> 07:23.360
We opened that cage
and the real man flies out.

07:23.880 --> 07:25.480
Reveals himself.

07:26.480 --> 07:29.720
The truth is young, Billy boy.

07:29.800 --> 07:31.880
Yeah. Yeah, look.

07:32.880 --> 07:34.400
What've we got here? Oh, look.

07:35.040 --> 07:38.560
Look at that, Billy boy, eh?
We got some snow here, look.

07:39.400 --> 07:41.920
Oh, there's some more.
Look, snowflakes, Billy.

07:42.480 --> 07:44.680
Now, I know you like that. Hmm?

07:44.760 --> 07:47.520
Well, I do, too. So I'll tell you what.

07:47.600 --> 07:49.800
Why don't we have
a little line together, eh?

07:49.880 --> 07:51.520
Why don't we do a bit of snow together?

07:51.600 --> 07:52.600
-[snorts]
-Ooh. [chuckles]

07:52.680 --> 07:57.560
Oh. I spilled it all down you an' all.
Messy, ain't I? Sorry, mate.

07:57.640 --> 08:01.560
What can I do? I'm messy, ain't I?
Billy, I do apologise. [sniffs]

08:01.640 --> 08:02.640
And you.

08:02.720 --> 08:03.640
[Finn] Hmm?

08:03.720 --> 08:05.000
Look at you.

08:05.080 --> 08:07.600
Sitting here with your mate,
eh, your best mate.

08:08.520 --> 08:12.080
Well, while you're sitting here
talking about our business,

08:12.160 --> 08:16.360
drinking whisky,
smoking and sniffing, hmm?

08:16.440 --> 08:17.480
I'm working.

08:17.560 --> 08:23.680
You remember, you tell this man
about our family business…

08:25.680 --> 08:27.640
and it's his life you're risking.

08:27.720 --> 08:29.560
'Cause people talk, Finn. Hmm?

08:29.640 --> 08:32.720
We… we only ever talk about
football and women, Mr Shelby.

08:33.520 --> 08:35.080
[Billy exhales heavily]

08:35.160 --> 08:38.039
We only ever-- We only ever
talk about football and women.

08:38.120 --> 08:39.880
-[Arthur] Oh, do you?
-Yeah.

08:39.960 --> 08:41.080
It's--

08:41.159 --> 08:43.640
[Arthur breathes deeply] Hmm.

08:44.720 --> 08:45.760
Yeah. Mm-hmm.

08:46.679 --> 08:47.520
Mm.

08:48.559 --> 08:49.640
Come.

08:50.360 --> 08:51.680
Family meeting. Let's go.

08:53.160 --> 08:54.320
[breathing shakily]

08:58.440 --> 08:59.440
[indistinct chatter]

09:01.040 --> 09:01.880
[door opens]

09:03.280 --> 09:05.440
[Arthur] You're not eating right.

09:05.520 --> 09:07.800
Getting the natural things in you.
That's what it is.

09:07.880 --> 09:09.160
Always.

09:09.720 --> 09:10.800
[Michael sighs]

09:16.000 --> 09:17.360
You bearing up, Arthur?

09:18.120 --> 09:19.920
[Arthur] Bearing up for what?

09:21.360 --> 09:23.000
Bearing up to be free, Pol.

09:26.400 --> 09:27.560
Another glass, eh?

09:28.080 --> 09:30.600
Another glass of "so what".

09:31.880 --> 09:32.720
[scoffs]

09:37.480 --> 09:38.880
Are you all right, Charlie?

09:40.200 --> 09:43.200
Mad bastard Barney kicked me in the shin
when I woke him up.

09:43.280 --> 09:45.080
Where is the mad bastard?

09:45.160 --> 09:46.160
[exhales heavily]

09:46.240 --> 09:48.800
He's tied to a lamppost outside
with three Lee boys,

09:48.880 --> 09:50.840
-shitting themselves.
-[Arthur grunts]

09:50.920 --> 09:51.920
[Curly] Right.

10:01.280 --> 10:02.360
[Tommy clears throat]

10:03.000 --> 10:04.080
First of all,

10:05.320 --> 10:09.200
an apology from Lizzie. She can't be here.

10:09.960 --> 10:13.000
Charles has a violin concert.

10:14.160 --> 10:17.920
Also, welcome to Mr Aberama Gold.

10:18.880 --> 10:22.560
He and Polly are to be married
in three weeks with my blessing.

10:23.320 --> 10:26.720
From now on,
Aberama will be welcome at our meetings.

10:28.120 --> 10:30.440
First item of business: a bereavement.

10:31.640 --> 10:33.120
Colonel Ben Younger,

10:33.640 --> 10:36.560
who may perhaps have
become a member of this family,

10:37.080 --> 10:42.520
was taken from us,
four days ago, by dark forces.

10:43.120 --> 10:47.040
We've made some investigations.
We think we know who planted the bomb.

10:47.640 --> 10:49.800
In the meantime,
our thoughts are with Ada,

10:50.520 --> 10:52.040
and the baby inside of her,

10:52.760 --> 10:56.440
who may one day
sit at these meetings, but…

10:57.400 --> 11:00.240
hopefully under happier circumstances.

11:00.320 --> 11:03.840
-Let's drink to happier circumstances.
-[Arthur] Yeah.

11:04.400 --> 11:05.440
[Aberama] Right.

11:05.520 --> 11:07.280
-To Ada.
-[men] Ada!

11:07.360 --> 11:08.920
-To Ada.
-[Michael] Ada.

11:11.640 --> 11:16.640
[coughs] Item number two:
an announcement regarding Michael.

11:16.720 --> 11:19.560
[clears throat] Before you go on, Tommy,

11:19.640 --> 11:23.160
there's something I'd like to say
to the whole family directly

11:23.800 --> 11:26.040
regarding finances
and the future of this company.

11:27.200 --> 11:29.240
According to your own estimations,

11:29.320 --> 11:33.040
this new venture
of the delivery and shipment of opium

11:33.120 --> 11:36.080
will bring into the company
around £2 million per year.

11:36.960 --> 11:40.360
Therefore, due to the amounts involved,

11:41.360 --> 11:43.160
I think this company
should be restructured.

11:43.240 --> 11:44.080
[Polly] Michael.

11:44.160 --> 11:46.960
I think this can wait
till outside the family meeting.

11:47.040 --> 11:48.400
Restructured in what way?

11:48.480 --> 11:50.360
[Gina] Because of the amounts
of money involved,

11:51.200 --> 11:52.040
shipment and dispatch

11:52.120 --> 11:54.920
will become the primary source
of income to the company.

11:55.000 --> 11:56.600
It's simple mathematics.

11:57.480 --> 12:01.680
With the help of my wife,
I will organise an expansion into America,

12:01.760 --> 12:04.400
where the narcotics business
is just beginning to grow.

12:05.240 --> 12:07.360
I have very good contacts in Detroit,

12:08.120 --> 12:11.400
New York, Boston,
who I've already spoken to about this.

12:12.040 --> 12:14.800
And Gina has family who are
very experienced in this kind of business.

12:16.080 --> 12:18.760
According to the conversations
I've had with them,

12:18.840 --> 12:22.040
with a regular supply
of pure opium from China,

12:22.120 --> 12:23.920
within a short space of time,

12:24.680 --> 12:30.320
the American narcotics business
will bring in $20 million per annum.

12:31.080 --> 12:36.280
Enough money for you to all enjoy
an easing of the burden you all now feel.

12:38.400 --> 12:42.520
See, I know that the scars and the wounds,

12:42.600 --> 12:46.040
they're on the inside, not on the outside.

12:46.120 --> 12:48.560
And as a member of the new generation,

12:48.640 --> 12:52.000
I am able to take that great burden
off your weary shoulders.

12:53.560 --> 12:55.080
A new decade is coming.

12:55.800 --> 12:58.680
There will be new opportunities
and new territories,

12:58.760 --> 13:00.680
more money than we've ever had before.

13:02.200 --> 13:03.480
Tommy,

13:04.360 --> 13:07.560
you can still do the good work
that deep down you want to do.

13:09.480 --> 13:13.000
Mum, you can get married
and live in that big house.

13:14.360 --> 13:16.800
Arthur, you can be the man
that Linda wants you to be.

13:16.880 --> 13:17.920
Fuck Linda.

13:20.840 --> 13:21.840
Finn.

13:23.400 --> 13:24.760
You've proved yourself.

13:26.800 --> 13:28.520
You're part of the new generation.

13:30.720 --> 13:32.520
You could come to New York with me.

13:36.600 --> 13:38.000
Here is my proposal.

13:40.160 --> 13:42.280
A full restructuring of the company.

13:43.200 --> 13:44.880
I will be managing director…

13:45.560 --> 13:47.760
and you can be non-executive chairman.

13:47.840 --> 13:51.040
But under an assumed name
to protect your reputation.

13:51.880 --> 13:56.080
I found the name of a dead man.
You will be registered as Mr Jones.

13:58.040 --> 14:01.480
You will each receive a percentage
of the profits as an annuity.

14:02.640 --> 14:08.000
And you will no longer have to engage
in any of the associated activities.

14:12.240 --> 14:13.920
Take a look at the future, Tommy.

14:16.080 --> 14:18.120
At least read it with an open mind.

14:25.920 --> 14:27.320
It's cold in here, Michael.

14:28.400 --> 14:29.400
[laughs]

14:29.480 --> 14:31.160
Tommy, the Americans want to deal with me.

14:31.240 --> 14:33.760
-Item number three--
-[Gina] Tell him the truth.

14:35.120 --> 14:36.160
Go on.

14:37.000 --> 14:38.040
He can take it.

14:44.840 --> 14:46.960
Tell me the truth, Michael.

14:49.640 --> 14:51.280
The Americans don't want to deal

14:51.360 --> 14:53.680
with an old-fashioned
backstreet razor gang.

14:54.280 --> 14:55.680
Those days are done.

14:56.520 --> 14:57.880
-[clamour in distance]
-[dog barks]

14:59.920 --> 15:02.560
Tommy, he's bitten
through the fucking rope.

15:02.640 --> 15:04.360
He's cornered, but they need help.

15:04.440 --> 15:05.800
Go and get him!

15:09.360 --> 15:10.800
Fuck the Americans.

15:12.280 --> 15:13.160
[men shouting]

15:22.120 --> 15:24.000
I'm doing this for you, Tommy.

15:25.840 --> 15:27.000
It's time…

15:28.680 --> 15:29.760
and you know it.

15:31.720 --> 15:36.760
Tommy, Mum's leaving.
John's dead. Arthur needs help.

15:37.360 --> 15:40.800
Ada's man was killed in your own backyard
because you fucked up.

15:42.640 --> 15:44.040
Go on, Tom.

15:44.920 --> 15:46.000
Go on, cut me.

15:46.920 --> 15:48.600
Like the good old days.

15:49.880 --> 15:50.880
Or…

15:52.520 --> 15:54.080
see this for what it is.

15:55.880 --> 16:00.120
A natural succession
that someday must happen.

16:01.560 --> 16:02.400
[smacks lips]

16:03.160 --> 16:04.440
[breathes deeply]

16:05.880 --> 16:08.840
I gave you an opportunity, Michael.
You betrayed me.

16:09.600 --> 16:11.120
Don't be here when I get back.

16:11.200 --> 16:12.200
You.

16:13.920 --> 16:16.080
-You can tell your family--
-Let me guess.

16:17.200 --> 16:18.960
Don't fuck with the Peaky Blinders.

16:22.120 --> 16:23.360
Right?

16:23.440 --> 16:24.280
[door opens]

16:26.480 --> 16:27.320
[door closes]

16:50.440 --> 16:51.920
-[door opens]
-[Gina clears throat]

16:53.000 --> 16:54.000
Well…

16:54.080 --> 16:55.120
[door closes]

16:55.200 --> 16:57.600
…guess we're gonna be forced
to take the second option.

17:02.160 --> 17:04.240
They're not fucking voices!

17:04.320 --> 17:06.360
Whoa! Whoa.

17:06.440 --> 17:07.480
Calm down.

17:07.560 --> 17:09.480
Put the gun down.

17:09.560 --> 17:12.240
-[Barney] They're not fucking voices!
-Barney!

17:12.319 --> 17:13.800
[man shouting indistinctly]

17:13.880 --> 17:14.839
[Tommy] Barney!

17:16.280 --> 17:18.960
Put down the gun. At ease.

17:20.119 --> 17:20.960
[grunts]

17:21.040 --> 17:22.119
Finn.

17:23.720 --> 17:25.040
At ease, soldier. At ease.

17:25.599 --> 17:27.319
-They're on our side.
-[heavy breathing]

17:27.880 --> 17:30.319
You're at home. You're at home.

17:30.960 --> 17:32.760
-Yeah? Yeah.
-[grunts and laughs]

17:32.839 --> 17:36.000
-[exhales heavily]
-Here. Take this, Barney. Jeremiah.

17:36.800 --> 17:37.720
Yeah.

17:38.280 --> 17:40.560
Take him to Charlie's yard
before he falls over.

17:40.640 --> 17:41.880
The devil will now be an angel.

17:41.960 --> 17:44.240
Isiah, Curly, you go with him.

17:44.320 --> 17:47.000
Come, brother.
Let me give you the good news.

17:47.080 --> 17:48.400
Jesus loves you.

17:49.560 --> 17:50.880
So, where the fuck is he?

17:50.960 --> 17:52.000
[Tommy] All right, boys.

17:52.080 --> 17:57.160
Subsidiary meeting of the generation
that actually do the work.

18:09.560 --> 18:10.400
[door closes]

18:11.520 --> 18:12.520
[Arthur] Right.

18:13.640 --> 18:16.840
Let's have the good stuff.
None of that shit the punters drink.

18:18.160 --> 18:19.840
Here we go.

18:19.920 --> 18:23.720
[coughs] All right, item number three:
an introduction.

18:24.480 --> 18:27.720
Except, now, you've already met the man
I was gonna introduce.

18:28.720 --> 18:30.440
In France, he was a comrade.

18:30.520 --> 18:34.440
-[chuckles] What the fuck is he now, Tom?
-He's a man we can use, Johnny.

18:34.520 --> 18:37.680
For what? Put him in a ring
with a bear and take bets on the outcome?

18:37.760 --> 18:41.200
I tell you, I wouldn't put much money
on the fucking bear. [chuckles]

18:42.000 --> 18:47.400
Aberama… that man
is a trained Royal Marines sniper.

18:48.120 --> 18:50.240
Furthermore, he has a criminal profile

18:50.320 --> 18:53.600
which will make his actions
explicable to the police.

18:54.320 --> 18:55.520
What actions?

18:56.400 --> 18:57.400
A killing.

18:58.120 --> 19:00.280
[Aberama] Since when
did you worry about the police?

19:03.040 --> 19:04.520
Barney Thomason

19:05.600 --> 19:07.160
is gonna kill an MP.

19:08.280 --> 19:10.640
Possibly the future prime minister
of Great Britain.

19:10.720 --> 19:12.480
What the fuck, Tom?

19:16.320 --> 19:17.160
[coughs]

19:17.840 --> 19:19.160
After the killing,

19:20.480 --> 19:24.120
there will be an investigation
by Special Branch and intelligence forces.

19:25.400 --> 19:28.880
There'll be a lot of powerful people
as angry as fucking hornets.

19:29.640 --> 19:31.760
We need there to be no connection to us.

19:32.440 --> 19:34.880
Barney Thomason is registered
as criminally insane.

19:34.960 --> 19:36.920
He broke out. He's an old soldier.

19:37.640 --> 19:39.320
He has known grievances.

19:39.400 --> 19:43.440
No one will question
that the assassination was carried out

19:43.520 --> 19:45.560
by a single gunman acting alone.

19:46.200 --> 19:49.240
And you'd sacrifice an old comrade?

19:50.000 --> 19:54.240
If they catch him, they won't hang him,
on grounds of insanity.

19:55.000 --> 19:56.840
Just send him back to where I found him.

19:57.640 --> 19:59.480
He'll have had a very eventful holiday

19:59.560 --> 20:01.400
that he'll probably believe
never happened.

20:02.120 --> 20:04.040
And where will this killing take place?

20:09.000 --> 20:10.000
There you go.

20:17.400 --> 20:18.680
He'll be onstage.

20:19.880 --> 20:20.840
With lots…

20:22.080 --> 20:23.320
of witnesses.

20:23.960 --> 20:28.320
[Tommy] During the rally, there will be
an anti-fascist demonstration.

20:29.040 --> 20:31.360
Amidst the confusion,
a shot will be fired.

20:31.440 --> 20:34.400
-And we're organising this demonstration?
-[Tommy] Yeah.

20:34.480 --> 20:36.160
Where will you be, Tom?

20:39.360 --> 20:41.960
I'll be down on one knee,
cradling his head

20:42.880 --> 20:44.560
while the life drains from him.

20:46.080 --> 20:47.680
And I'll make a speech,

20:48.600 --> 20:51.360
saying how the cause he died for
must continue.

20:52.760 --> 20:54.400
Continue safe in my hands.

20:55.640 --> 20:56.800
[Aberama] Holy fuck.

20:58.520 --> 21:02.760
Tommy, does your ambition have no limits?

21:05.040 --> 21:05.880
[inhales]

21:05.960 --> 21:09.120
Jimmy McCavern will be
running security at this event.

21:09.960 --> 21:11.640
He'll probably be in the wings.

21:12.680 --> 21:15.480
You can take his life,
whichever manner you choose.

21:20.320 --> 21:21.640
What do you want us to do, Tom?

21:22.240 --> 21:24.160
You and Arthur
and a couple of the Lee boys

21:24.240 --> 21:26.960
will be in charge
of getting Barney into position.

21:27.040 --> 21:28.600
He'll be up in the lighting gantry.

21:29.400 --> 21:33.160
-We'll need chains and a twitch, Tom.
-No, I will medicate him.

21:33.840 --> 21:36.760
So he's gonna be cross-eyed
when he takes his shot.

21:37.480 --> 21:40.240
In France, he never missed.

21:41.240 --> 21:42.800
No matter what they gave him.

21:44.000 --> 21:46.080
He'll have had plenty of target practice.

21:46.600 --> 21:51.320
Before he takes the shot,
Arthur here will give him some cocaine.

21:51.400 --> 21:53.640
-Sharpen him up.
-[chuckles] So, just…

21:54.320 --> 21:56.080
You're gonna be up on the stage

21:56.160 --> 21:59.240
while this criminally-insane gunman
filled with cocaine

21:59.320 --> 22:02.680
takes aim at a man
just a yard away from you?

22:04.680 --> 22:06.320
Welcome to the family, Aberama.

22:06.840 --> 22:10.600
What about me, Thomas?
The man with the broken fucking leg.

22:11.400 --> 22:12.280
[inhales sharply]

22:12.840 --> 22:14.320
After the killing,

22:14.400 --> 22:17.240
every copper in Birmingham
will be sent to Bingley Hall.

22:18.120 --> 22:20.040
Use that opportunity

22:20.120 --> 22:23.600
to get that boat full of opium
up to Stourbridge Locks.

22:24.400 --> 22:28.080
There, you'll be met
by some Chinese gentlemen.

22:28.880 --> 22:31.120
They will have two suitcases full of cash.

22:32.440 --> 22:34.480
£250,000.

22:35.040 --> 22:35.920
[inhales sharply]

22:36.400 --> 22:40.640
Every man in this room will receive
£30,000 in cash

22:40.720 --> 22:42.680
in recognition of extra services.

22:43.240 --> 22:47.800
Holy Mary, mother of God, Tom.
Good man. [chuckles]

22:47.880 --> 22:51.400
[Tommy] Anyone who wants
to leave, leave now.

22:52.560 --> 22:59.480
Anyone who is tired of this old-fashioned,
backstreet fucking razor gang can leave.

23:00.400 --> 23:03.360
Anyone who is tired can fucking stop.

23:08.600 --> 23:09.600
Good.

23:10.600 --> 23:14.600
Charlie, go to the yard and light a fire.

23:14.680 --> 23:16.160
Johnny, bring the van around.

23:17.560 --> 23:19.120
What's the fire for, Tom?

23:21.480 --> 23:23.120
There is an item number four.

23:23.200 --> 23:24.120
[Dogs chuckles]

23:31.720 --> 23:32.560
[door closes]

23:38.400 --> 23:39.240
[door opens]

23:42.080 --> 23:42.920
[door closes]

23:44.720 --> 23:45.760
It's time.

24:00.800 --> 24:02.440
[door unlocks and opens]

24:03.640 --> 24:04.480
[keys jangling]

24:05.520 --> 24:06.560
[man humming]

24:07.120 --> 24:07.960
[door closes]

24:12.680 --> 24:14.000
Jeez, Mr Shelby.

24:14.720 --> 24:17.720
Well, if I'd known, I'd have come in early
and served you drinks, huh?

24:21.680 --> 24:22.720
Here, Micky.

24:25.960 --> 24:27.000
Sit down there.

24:46.360 --> 24:47.880
Sure, I'll have a drink, will I?

24:52.040 --> 24:53.440
Here you go, have a drink.

25:01.240 --> 25:03.000
A few days ago, I went to London, Micky…

25:05.600 --> 25:06.560
[sniffs]

25:06.640 --> 25:08.040
…to collect some cargo.

25:11.240 --> 25:13.440
I was met by the Titanic boys.

25:13.520 --> 25:14.840
[clears throat] Hmm.

25:16.280 --> 25:18.360
They knew I was coming. Hmm.

25:19.480 --> 25:20.480
Yeah.

25:20.560 --> 25:22.960
When, where… what time.

25:23.760 --> 25:27.480
They even knew the cargo I was picking up.

25:27.560 --> 25:28.400
[Micky] Jesus.

25:29.000 --> 25:30.720
Four days ago, Micky,

25:31.480 --> 25:37.840
a soldier was killed outside my office
by a bomb.

25:37.920 --> 25:40.920
Yeah, erm…
the papers said that was the IRA.

25:41.480 --> 25:46.120
-That wasn't the IRA, Micky.
-No. It weren't the IRA, Micky.

25:49.600 --> 25:55.600
I spoke to the girls who work
at the Digbeth telephone exchange.

25:55.680 --> 25:56.920
They're friends of mine.

25:59.200 --> 26:00.880
[coughs] I asked 'em…

26:02.480 --> 26:05.160
what calls were made
around the time of the explosion.

26:07.040 --> 26:08.640
They told me that…

26:10.680 --> 26:15.000
thirty minutes before the explosion,
a call was made to a man in Sparkhill

26:15.080 --> 26:17.880
who has connections
to the Ulster Volunteer Force.

26:18.400 --> 26:20.640
He now offers his services for cash.

26:26.720 --> 26:27.880
Paddy Rose.

26:32.640 --> 26:37.280
Yeah, me and me brother,
we spoke to Paddy at length.

26:38.680 --> 26:41.600
He told us it was him
that planted the bomb.

26:43.560 --> 26:44.760
Yeah, we spoke to him.

26:49.560 --> 26:51.520
We killed him, Micky.

26:53.320 --> 26:54.760
Paddy Rose is dead.

26:54.840 --> 26:56.160
We weighed him down…

26:56.920 --> 27:01.440
we sunk him…
to the bottom of the Grand Union Canal.

27:01.520 --> 27:02.360
[Tommy sighs]

27:07.000 --> 27:09.160
The girls at the exchange
gave me the number

27:09.240 --> 27:11.760
of the man that called, Micky,
before the explosion.

27:11.840 --> 27:13.000
That was your number.

27:14.840 --> 27:15.840
Micky…

27:16.880 --> 27:20.560
it was you who called him,
who tipped him off.

27:20.640 --> 27:21.520
[breathes deeply]

27:22.960 --> 27:23.960
You were told to call him

27:24.040 --> 27:26.920
if a Black man of a certain description
ever came to Small Heath.

27:28.240 --> 27:29.520
[Micky breathing shakily]

27:34.200 --> 27:38.320
We know you've been giving
the Titanic boys information as well.

27:38.400 --> 27:39.480
Hmm?

27:39.560 --> 27:40.600
We know that.

27:41.840 --> 27:42.720
Yeah.

27:43.520 --> 27:45.840
You've been working behind the bar, hmm?

27:46.600 --> 27:50.160
Seeing what goes on,
listening, taking notes,

27:51.040 --> 27:54.880
and selling your stories
to the highest bidder. Hmm?

27:54.960 --> 27:55.800
[Tommy sighs]

28:00.760 --> 28:01.640
Come on.

28:01.720 --> 28:02.560
[Micky whimpers]

28:04.400 --> 28:05.360
Come on, man.

28:07.240 --> 28:08.080
[crying]

28:16.120 --> 28:16.960
[mumbling]

28:29.360 --> 28:30.840
I am sorry, Mr Shelby.

28:38.760 --> 28:40.320
Don't look at Tommy.

28:45.480 --> 28:47.520
The ceiling'd be cheaper, brother.

28:48.640 --> 28:49.760
Micky!

28:56.640 --> 28:57.480
[gasps]

29:02.520 --> 29:04.280
Fucking hell, Arthur.

29:04.960 --> 29:05.920
Eh?

29:06.000 --> 29:07.640
Shaking like the hand of a normal man.

29:15.320 --> 29:18.720
What about item five, Tom? Hmm?

29:20.480 --> 29:23.640
[shakily] There is an item five,
right? Tommy?

29:24.200 --> 29:25.280
[sighs]

29:25.360 --> 29:27.160
I'm fucking sinking here, man.

29:28.600 --> 29:29.440
[sobbing]

29:31.160 --> 29:32.760
I'm fucking sinking, Tom.

29:34.320 --> 29:37.400
You said there's an item five.
Say it, Tommy.

29:37.480 --> 29:38.440
[Tommy sighs heavily]

29:38.520 --> 29:41.400
Maybe item five can start now, Tommy.

29:42.240 --> 29:45.720
It could start this year, a new decade,

29:46.680 --> 29:51.520
but Michael… Michael could be right.
We could go, Tommy. We could go.

29:52.400 --> 29:56.560
We could fucking leave this place.
Leave it to the kids.

29:56.640 --> 29:58.920
Michael is… He might be right.

29:59.640 --> 30:04.920
-He might be fucking right--
-Arthur, there is no item number five!

30:17.840 --> 30:20.080
Go and check
that Polly is still on our side.

30:21.160 --> 30:22.400
I have to go to Margate.

30:22.960 --> 30:23.920
All right, Tom.

30:27.160 --> 30:28.200
All right, brother.

30:28.880 --> 30:33.160
♪ I got one more wish before I die ♪

30:34.880 --> 30:36.200
Oh, God. Jesus Christ.

30:37.320 --> 30:38.440
[song playing over speaker]

30:38.520 --> 30:42.040
♪ So, please, don't you stop me
No, don't you stop me ♪

30:42.120 --> 30:45.760
♪ I got one more wish before I die ♪

30:50.880 --> 30:54.760
♪ So, please, don't you stop me
No, don't you stop me ♪

30:56.440 --> 30:57.760
[Alfie] You out there, Tommy?

31:00.080 --> 31:01.760
[Tommy] Yeah. I'm here.

31:02.640 --> 31:06.920
[Alfie] I was just having some oil rubbed
into the bits that really hurt, mate.

31:08.600 --> 31:10.280
What do you think of that view, eh?

31:11.920 --> 31:13.840
[Tommy] It's Margate. What can you do?

31:13.920 --> 31:17.880
♪ …don't you stop me
I got one more wish before I-- ♪

31:17.960 --> 31:20.080
-[song stops playing]
-I'll tell you something,

31:20.160 --> 31:23.960
I sit all day, every day,
in that chair on that balcony,

31:24.040 --> 31:26.240
contemplating the fact, right,

31:26.920 --> 31:30.520
that life is so much easier to deal with
when you are dead.

31:31.840 --> 31:32.680
[grunts]

31:34.960 --> 31:36.120
Hello, Alfie.

31:36.640 --> 31:39.440
Yeah. Did you…
Did you look through the binoculars?

31:39.520 --> 31:40.360
Yeah.

31:40.440 --> 31:43.480
I watch ships. No two are the same. Yeah.

31:44.760 --> 31:47.640
That is how God sees us both in his eyes.

31:48.160 --> 31:49.560
"God", eh?

31:49.640 --> 31:51.240
Yeah, sort of. I mean, you know…

31:51.320 --> 31:54.280
Someone's responsible
for all this fucking mess.

31:55.640 --> 31:59.520
Now, how soon did you know
that I was not dead?

31:59.600 --> 32:02.480
-You wrote me a letter, Alfie.
-Did I?

32:02.560 --> 32:04.520
Yeah, you asked about your dog.

32:05.360 --> 32:09.800
Oh. They gave me a lot of drugs
at first, yeah… [mutters]

32:10.920 --> 32:15.840
I was lying out there,
and the tide come in and woke me up.

32:16.600 --> 32:19.600
I remember looking around
and thinking, you know,

32:20.720 --> 32:21.880
"Fuck.

32:22.920 --> 32:24.400
"If this is hell…

32:26.120 --> 32:28.040
then it looks a lot like Margate."

32:28.680 --> 32:30.880
Maybe that's just what
hell looks like, eh?

32:30.960 --> 32:34.840
No. No. Not according
to this holy book right here, yeah.

32:34.920 --> 32:38.080
It gives a very, very vivid description.

32:38.160 --> 32:40.560
You and I are both fucked, mate.

32:44.240 --> 32:47.680
-You read the papers, Alfie?
-No. Don't be silly.

32:47.760 --> 32:48.920
[gun cocking]

32:49.000 --> 32:52.000
-But you've heard.
-What? Fascism, yeah?

32:55.040 --> 32:59.040
Three, two, one…

33:00.200 --> 33:01.240
bang.

33:01.920 --> 33:02.880
No?

33:04.680 --> 33:05.560
Fine.

33:07.080 --> 33:10.240
Good Lord, your fucking condition
has got worse, mate.

33:10.320 --> 33:11.400
[coughs]

33:11.480 --> 33:14.480
Mine, on the other hand, I…
I've been living the dream.

33:14.560 --> 33:17.480
Sometimes, I will shoot
at the side of a ship,

33:17.560 --> 33:21.200
and sometimes, I'll sit here,
I may shoot at the old seagull.

33:21.280 --> 33:22.280
Alfie…

33:24.080 --> 33:24.920
[exhales]

33:25.000 --> 33:26.920
I'm gonna shoot Oswald Mosley.

33:27.560 --> 33:28.680
Right. Well…

33:29.520 --> 33:32.960
I hope you do a better job on him
than the one you done on me, yeah?

33:34.240 --> 33:38.680
[stammers] I mean, what were you thinking?
Was your mind somewhere else, Tommy?

33:40.240 --> 33:41.560
Yes, it was, actually.

33:42.200 --> 33:44.840
-Yeah. All right.
-[ship horn blares]

33:46.000 --> 33:47.160
Oh, look.

33:48.560 --> 33:49.520
A ship.

33:57.000 --> 33:58.800
Why do you want to shoot him?

33:59.600 --> 34:02.520
I need to organise a riot, Alfie.

34:02.600 --> 34:03.520
All right.

34:03.600 --> 34:09.440
And I hear you still have some…
standing in the Jewish community.

34:10.400 --> 34:12.680
Let me be clear, all right?

34:13.639 --> 34:19.800
Since my resurrection,
I am considered to be a god, all right?

34:19.880 --> 34:24.600
In the Holy Land,
someone has made an image of me

34:24.679 --> 34:27.639
out of rock embedded in the sand,
so I am told,

34:27.719 --> 34:31.679
and I am planning to make a pilgrimage
to stand in my own shadow.

34:37.000 --> 34:40.239
Are you gonna shoot him
because this man is evil?

34:40.920 --> 34:42.480
I need men who can fight.

34:43.800 --> 34:46.600
Mosley uses men from Glasgow.

34:47.360 --> 34:51.639
So, if the men causing the trouble
are Jewish, it will be… explicable.

34:51.719 --> 34:54.120
Since when do you
need explanations, Tommy?

34:54.199 --> 34:56.120
Since I entered politics.

34:56.199 --> 35:00.920
Oh, that's right, yeah. Oh, yeah.
And how has that been for you, Tom?

35:02.080 --> 35:06.240
Gangs, wars, truces…
Nothing I didn't already know.

35:06.920 --> 35:07.760
[Alfie snores]

35:11.080 --> 35:16.960
So, you think if you kill him,
you will kill the message, yeah?

35:17.760 --> 35:21.360
I will kill the man,
then I will kill the message.

35:22.480 --> 35:23.320
[sighs heavily]

35:25.760 --> 35:26.960
How much you paying?

35:28.280 --> 35:29.880
Thought you might do it for the cause.

35:29.960 --> 35:31.360
Go on, fuck off.

35:32.000 --> 35:35.360
Each man will get £20. You'll get £5,000.

35:35.440 --> 35:37.520
You know, as a god, Tommy, right,

35:37.600 --> 35:43.360
I am now able to just rise
above those kinds of insults, mate.

35:44.240 --> 35:46.440
-Ten? [sighs]
-Hmm.

35:48.440 --> 35:49.840
How is my dog?

35:50.880 --> 35:53.040
-Your dog is fine.
-Hmm.

35:55.120 --> 35:57.880
In that case, ten should be enough.
Where do you want the men?

35:57.960 --> 35:58.880
Birmingham.

35:58.960 --> 36:00.120
No. No.

36:00.200 --> 36:04.520
That 20 will not be enough for my lads
to step inside that fucking shithole.

36:04.600 --> 36:07.360
It'll have to be 25, at least.

36:07.440 --> 36:08.280
[inhales]

36:08.360 --> 36:11.200
Twenty-five it is.
You can take your dog back then, eh?

36:11.280 --> 36:14.080
No, it is better for him
to think that I am still dead.

36:15.320 --> 36:17.360
As it is also with the police.

36:21.320 --> 36:22.440
All right.

36:22.520 --> 36:25.760
So, you're still at it, eh, Tommy? Hmm.

36:26.520 --> 36:28.880
Ain't got no Margate to go to.

36:28.960 --> 36:30.120
[tuts]

36:31.040 --> 36:31.960
No.

36:34.320 --> 36:36.480
I have no interest in shooting seagulls.

36:36.560 --> 36:39.440
Oh, but you have in shooting
cabinet ministers.

36:39.520 --> 36:40.400
Yeah.

36:41.800 --> 36:43.480
And their paid informants.

36:43.560 --> 36:44.400
[Alfie] Mm.

36:47.240 --> 36:50.200
I was on a lot of drugs at first, right,

36:50.280 --> 36:52.880
due to the pain, you know,
on account of it…

36:53.440 --> 36:58.720
well, you know,
being shot in the face by some cunt.

36:58.800 --> 37:01.960
I won't bore you with the details.
It'd chill ya.

37:02.040 --> 37:05.360
Nonetheless, I had a recurring dream.

37:06.720 --> 37:11.600
I saw you in a field, right,
with a big black horse,

37:11.680 --> 37:16.560
and you said, "Goodbye", and then, bang.

37:27.120 --> 37:28.640
All right, then, well…

37:29.360 --> 37:30.520
what now?

37:36.680 --> 37:37.520
[sighs]

37:40.360 --> 37:41.200
[smacks lips]

37:44.080 --> 37:45.240
I will continue…

37:47.560 --> 37:49.000
till I find a man…

37:49.960 --> 37:51.320
that I can't defeat.

37:55.240 --> 37:56.080
[Alfie] Hmm.

38:22.160 --> 38:24.240
[Polly] Arthur asked whose side I was on.

38:36.880 --> 38:37.760
[exhales]

38:40.400 --> 38:44.600
There will be a war
and one of you will die.

38:44.680 --> 38:45.560
[breathes deeply]

38:46.200 --> 38:48.240
But which one, I cannot tell.

38:50.080 --> 38:50.920
Hmm.

38:53.760 --> 38:55.280
He's gonna do it anyway.

38:56.560 --> 38:57.440
Yeah.

38:58.280 --> 38:59.520
You should know,

39:00.080 --> 39:02.720
if Aberama takes his side,
I will kill him.

39:06.480 --> 39:07.840
What about me?

39:11.320 --> 39:12.960
I'll do what I have to do, Pol.

39:15.320 --> 39:18.920
Kill and kill…

39:20.120 --> 39:21.960
The only way to make people listen.

39:34.400 --> 39:37.080
Soon, you will have a stage to stand on,

39:38.680 --> 39:42.200
millions of people will listen to you,

39:43.640 --> 39:48.160
and you will run the country
like you run this family.

39:49.560 --> 39:51.520
It appears to be what people want.

39:52.640 --> 39:53.720
But not me.

39:54.960 --> 39:56.120
Not anymore.

39:57.080 --> 39:58.800
My resignation.

40:08.400 --> 40:09.240
[door opens]

40:11.160 --> 40:12.000
[door closes]

40:26.040 --> 40:28.120
♪ You walk into the room ♪

40:29.160 --> 40:31.440
♪ With your pencil in your hand ♪

40:32.680 --> 40:37.920
♪ You see somebody naked
And you say, "Who is that man?" ♪

40:39.160 --> 40:44.120
♪ You try so hard
But you don't understand ♪

40:44.200 --> 40:45.320
[phone ringing]

40:45.400 --> 40:49.800
♪ Just what you will say
When you get home ♪

40:49.880 --> 40:50.720
[phone ringing]

40:52.040 --> 40:57.440
♪ Because something is happening here
But you don't know what it is ♪

40:58.760 --> 41:03.360
♪ Do you, Mr Jones? ♪

41:05.480 --> 41:06.520
[phone ringing]

41:08.600 --> 41:14.280
♪ You raise up your head
And you ask, "Is this where it is?" ♪

41:15.080 --> 41:17.960
♪ And somebody points to you and says ♪

41:18.040 --> 41:18.880
[phone ringing]

41:18.960 --> 41:20.320
♪ "It's his" ♪

41:21.320 --> 41:26.960
♪ And you say, "What's mine?"
And somebody else says, "Well, what is?" ♪

41:27.040 --> 41:31.920
♪ And you say, "Oh, my God
Am I here all alone?" ♪

41:42.640 --> 41:45.320
[Charlie] If it's Barney
you're worried about, he's sleeping.

41:45.400 --> 41:48.080
But I can't sleep,
'cause my fucking leg is cracked.

42:05.160 --> 42:08.040
Tell me how me mother went, Charlie.
[clears throat]

42:12.000 --> 42:15.120
You know. She drowned.

42:18.400 --> 42:20.080
I know it wasn't by accident.

42:24.440 --> 42:25.360
[exhales heavily]

42:28.960 --> 42:31.680
-Tell me the truth, Charlie.
-The truth, Tommy, yeah?

42:32.360 --> 42:33.920
The fucking truth.

42:39.760 --> 42:40.880
Fuck's sake.

42:52.280 --> 42:54.080
She just stepped into the canal.

42:57.560 --> 42:59.040
Your dad was no use.

43:00.040 --> 43:02.240
It was me trying to stop her
for three days.

43:04.520 --> 43:06.200
In the end, she did it anyway.

43:11.880 --> 43:14.720
-Did she say why?
-Nothing that made sense.

43:17.080 --> 43:19.160
Tell me the things that didn't make sense.

43:22.160 --> 43:25.440
She said it were the gypsies
made the nails for Jesus' cross,

43:25.520 --> 43:27.400
and that's why we're cursed and restless.

43:29.640 --> 43:30.600
Yeah, go on.

43:31.600 --> 43:34.480
You have to move around
or the guilt catches up with you.

43:37.000 --> 43:39.600
I said, "Well, why not go
on the road for a bit?"

43:46.280 --> 43:47.560
She went to Worcester.

43:48.920 --> 43:50.840
She came back with a white pony.

43:56.920 --> 43:58.520
The one she gave to you.

44:01.640 --> 44:04.080
You used to ride it around, remember?

44:08.560 --> 44:11.240
Well, she seemed happy for a bit,
watching you ride it.

44:14.880 --> 44:16.040
And then she was gone.

44:19.520 --> 44:21.160
None of it made any sense.

44:23.800 --> 44:26.960
Afterwards, whenever I looked
at that white pony, I saw her.

44:33.240 --> 44:35.440
You see, I was in love with her, Tom.

44:37.560 --> 44:38.800
No one knew but me.

44:41.640 --> 44:44.760
Broke my fucking heart
to pull her from the cut.

44:49.520 --> 44:50.360
[sniffles]

44:50.440 --> 44:54.240
You know, your grandfather,
he went the same way. Suicide.

44:55.320 --> 44:57.520
Sometimes, these things run in the family.

45:01.040 --> 45:02.440
Fuck family, Tom.

45:03.680 --> 45:05.280
You just have to get on with it.

45:05.360 --> 45:09.040
You're a Gypsy. You have to move around,
or it all catches up with you.

45:10.360 --> 45:14.360
♪ There ain't no grave ♪

45:16.040 --> 45:17.080
[sniffles]

45:17.160 --> 45:23.080
♪ Can hold my body down ♪

45:49.280 --> 45:50.120
[exclaims]

45:55.560 --> 45:56.880
Didn't need all them tablets.

45:57.800 --> 45:59.800
You just needed another fucking war, eh?

46:06.680 --> 46:07.520
♪ Hey, hey ♪

46:09.880 --> 46:13.640
♪ I'm council house and violent
I'm laughing at the tyrants ♪

46:13.720 --> 46:17.560
♪ I'm sleeping under sirens
Whilst wondering where the time went ♪

46:17.640 --> 46:22.280
♪ I'm scum, I'm scum, yeah ♪

46:23.600 --> 46:24.480
♪ Hey, hey ♪

46:25.640 --> 46:26.520
♪ Hey, hey ♪

46:27.680 --> 46:28.560
♪ Hey, hey ♪

46:29.840 --> 46:31.880
-Perish Judah.
-Perish Judah!

46:31.960 --> 46:34.640
♪ …fascists till my head comes off ♪

46:35.320 --> 46:38.720
♪ I am Dennis Skinner's Molotov ♪

46:38.800 --> 46:39.720
Hello!

46:39.800 --> 46:40.640
Shalom!

46:41.160 --> 46:42.680
My friends, shalom!

46:43.200 --> 46:44.200
[indistinct greeting]

46:44.880 --> 46:46.680
♪ I'm just another cunt ♪

46:46.760 --> 46:51.120
♪ I'm scum, I'm scum, yeah ♪

46:52.640 --> 46:53.640
♪ Hey, hey ♪

46:54.680 --> 46:55.600
♪ Hey, hey ♪

46:56.800 --> 46:57.720
♪ Hey, hey ♪

47:00.120 --> 47:03.760
♪ This snowflake's an avalanche ♪

47:03.840 --> 47:07.640
♪ Dirty martyred filthy scum ♪

47:08.200 --> 47:10.840
Show these fascist bastards
no mercy, brothers.

47:11.920 --> 47:12.760
[moans]

47:14.000 --> 47:16.320
Jew and the Gypsy united.

47:16.400 --> 47:20.160
-Look, I have to go, yeah? I have to go.
-Go where?

47:20.240 --> 47:23.360
-They're shooting a fascist tonight.
-They're gonna do what?

47:23.920 --> 47:24.760
[shushes]

47:27.200 --> 47:29.600
-Mosley's in town.
-Really?

47:29.680 --> 47:35.120
[sniffles] Look, go into town,
get some drink and some girl

47:35.200 --> 47:36.840
and listen to the radio.

47:36.920 --> 47:38.880
[indistinct shouting on radio]

47:38.960 --> 47:39.840
[door opens]

47:40.480 --> 47:41.320
[door closes]

47:43.920 --> 47:44.760
[sighs]

47:48.600 --> 47:52.920
We will not stand by and let this scum
have free rein in our city!

47:53.000 --> 47:56.880
Fascism must not be allowed
to voice its creed of hatred!

47:57.440 --> 47:59.040
[crowd shouting and clamouring]

48:02.440 --> 48:03.320
[whistle blowing]

48:03.920 --> 48:06.200
[Arthur] Get out the fucking way.

48:07.760 --> 48:10.200
[Jessie] We have a right to protest!

48:11.680 --> 48:14.760
Anybody heckles,
you beat the fuck out of them.

48:14.840 --> 48:16.160
["Rule Britannia" playing]

48:42.960 --> 48:45.240
[Jessie] We have a right to protest!

48:45.320 --> 48:46.960
[officers speaking indistinctly]

48:47.600 --> 48:48.840
[officer 1] Calm yourself down.

48:50.400 --> 48:52.240
It's not against the law to protest.

48:55.760 --> 48:57.400
[officer 2] Out of the way.

48:57.480 --> 48:58.320
[Tommy] Let her go.

48:58.400 --> 49:00.280
I don't need the help of a fascist.

49:00.360 --> 49:01.200
Yes, you do.

49:01.280 --> 49:03.520
At Steelhouse Lane,
they'll do whatever they want to you.

49:03.600 --> 49:04.440
Let her go.

49:05.760 --> 49:08.280
I'm Tommy Shelby, and I'm ordering you
to let her fucking go.

49:08.360 --> 49:09.360
Go on.

49:10.600 --> 49:11.920
Fuck you.

49:12.000 --> 49:12.840
Jessie.

49:13.640 --> 49:15.440
We can do more damage from the inside.

49:16.360 --> 49:17.360
Understand?

49:18.200 --> 49:20.520
We can do more damage from the inside.

49:22.280 --> 49:23.120
Come on.

49:23.640 --> 49:24.960
-Come on.
-[clamouring continues]

49:25.040 --> 49:25.880
Out of the way.

49:26.440 --> 49:27.280
Out of the way.

49:31.400 --> 49:33.360
Here, look. A little.

49:34.600 --> 49:35.440
[snorts]

49:38.240 --> 49:39.160
I'll join ya.

49:40.000 --> 49:40.840
-Oh.
-[exhales]

49:41.480 --> 49:42.880
-Gallipoli, eh?
-Yeah.

49:42.960 --> 49:44.200
You know what you're doing?

49:44.280 --> 49:47.520
Yeah, Tommy checks his pocket watch,
I count to ten,

49:47.600 --> 49:49.320
then I blow the other bloke's head off.

49:49.400 --> 49:50.640
-Yeah.
-Yeah?

49:50.720 --> 49:51.560
-Yeah.
-Yeah?

49:51.640 --> 49:53.160
-That's for after.
-Thank you.

49:53.240 --> 49:54.760
-All right.
-Thank you.

49:54.840 --> 49:56.840
-See you later, Arthur.
-Oh, soldier…

49:56.920 --> 49:59.000
Soldier, you're meant to…

49:59.080 --> 50:02.240
-You run like fuck. Don't stop.
-Run like fuck.

50:02.320 --> 50:03.680
-Yeah.
-Run like fuck.

50:04.960 --> 50:05.800
[bangs door]

50:16.840 --> 50:17.880
In here.

50:21.400 --> 50:24.480
-Here, for your face.
-At least I have only one face.

50:25.560 --> 50:27.840
What did you mean,
"damage from the inside"?

50:27.920 --> 50:30.720
-I have a strategy.
-You always have a strategy.

50:30.800 --> 50:31.960
But it's dangerous,

50:32.040 --> 50:34.840
and it can't be shared
without sharing the danger.

50:34.920 --> 50:36.360
-You think I'm afraid?
-No.

50:36.440 --> 50:39.080
That's only gonna put you in more danger.

50:39.160 --> 50:42.440
Jessie, before the speeches start,
just go home.

50:42.520 --> 50:45.680
There's gonna be lots of arrests.
You have a mark against your name.

50:45.760 --> 50:48.560
Why? What's going to happen?

50:53.880 --> 50:55.320
I'm gonna do a good thing.

50:56.760 --> 51:00.440
Whenever I do a good thing,
innocent people get hurt.

51:01.000 --> 51:02.040
So go home.

51:03.120 --> 51:05.960
After this evening,
we can meet, discuss strategy.

51:06.520 --> 51:07.440
That beast…

51:08.240 --> 51:09.720
out there, he's just a beast.

51:10.320 --> 51:11.360
He's like a horse.

51:12.040 --> 51:14.800
It's the rider that decides
what direction it takes.

51:16.760 --> 51:18.200
And who will be the rider?

51:19.920 --> 51:21.280
Just go home.

51:23.160 --> 51:24.000
[door closes]

51:30.720 --> 51:33.600
-[Mosley] Full?
-[McCavern] To the fucking brim.

51:34.840 --> 51:37.880
-Trouble?
-So far, a few communists.

51:39.000 --> 51:41.280
Bowlers helped our boys clear them away.

51:41.800 --> 51:44.200
A few hecklers are a good thing.

51:44.280 --> 51:46.800
We can illustrate
how we deal with opposition.

51:46.880 --> 51:50.840
There's a rumour a gang of Jews
are coming up from Digbeth.

51:50.920 --> 51:52.080
No sign of them yet.

51:52.840 --> 51:56.040
Well, let them come.
Welcome them appropriately.

51:59.360 --> 52:01.400
There are a few Peaky boys around.

52:03.120 --> 52:06.440
They are your allies.
There'll be no rifts between us.

52:07.000 --> 52:08.640
Keep your powder dry.

52:15.680 --> 52:17.120
Mr McCavern.

52:20.040 --> 52:20.960
Perish Judah.

52:21.040 --> 52:21.880
[scoffs]

52:22.480 --> 52:24.520
No joke, Mr McCavern.

52:29.400 --> 52:30.320
Perish Judah.

52:39.800 --> 52:41.480
["Pomp and Circumstance" playing]

52:42.720 --> 52:44.400
[audience applauding and cheering]

53:31.320 --> 53:33.960
Will you turn the radio on,
and turn the volume up?

53:35.280 --> 53:36.960
I wanna listen to the news.

53:40.720 --> 53:44.240
[announcer] Ladies and gentlemen,
Mr Oswald Mosley.

53:44.320 --> 53:45.320
[audience cheering]

53:47.440 --> 53:53.280
♪ A heathen from Eton
On a bag of Michael Keaton ♪

53:54.160 --> 53:58.120
Perish Judah! Perish Judah! Perish Judah!

53:59.760 --> 54:01.520
♪ He thinks he's suave ♪

54:01.600 --> 54:04.680
♪ You're not suave
'Cause you watched Get Carter ♪

54:04.760 --> 54:07.400
♪ You are a catalogue, plastic Sinatra ♪

54:07.480 --> 54:10.960
♪ A tryhard who should've tried harder ♪

54:11.640 --> 54:14.320
♪ Me, oh, me, oh, my, Roy ♪

54:14.400 --> 54:17.720
♪ You look like a walking thyroid ♪

54:17.800 --> 54:19.840
♪ You're not a man, you're a gland ♪

54:19.920 --> 54:23.320
♪ You're one big neck with sausage hands ♪

54:23.960 --> 54:26.920
♪ You are a Topshop tyrant ♪

54:27.000 --> 54:29.640
♪ Even your haircut's violent ♪

54:29.720 --> 54:32.680
♪ You look like you're from Love Island ♪

54:32.760 --> 54:35.680
♪ He stood and the room went silent ♪

54:35.760 --> 54:37.240
[audience continues chanting]

54:42.840 --> 54:48.280
♪ Never fight a man with a perm ♪

54:52.320 --> 54:53.640
[microphone feedback]

54:53.720 --> 54:56.960
Welcome, men and women of Birmingham.

54:58.560 --> 55:01.600
Thank you for coming here
on this cold, dark night

55:01.680 --> 55:05.760
in spite of the obstruction
and provocation of our enemies.

55:06.680 --> 55:11.760
Our enemies deal in bricks
and stones and bottles.

55:11.840 --> 55:16.120
We deal in reasoned principle,
argument and fact.

55:16.200 --> 55:17.040
[audience applauds]

55:17.120 --> 55:21.600
Among those enemies,
we can number Mr Winston Churchill…

55:22.360 --> 55:26.720
who, last night, condemned me in the House
as a threat to democracy.

55:26.800 --> 55:28.280
[audience jeers]

55:33.880 --> 55:37.560
Thems who've gone are the lucky ones.
Thems who've gone are the lucky ones.

55:41.160 --> 55:45.360
But then, Mr Churchill has never been
a friend of the common people.

55:46.400 --> 55:50.800
Faced with the alternative
of saying goodbye to the gold standard

55:50.880 --> 55:56.440
and, therefore, to his own employment,
he characteristically selected the latter.

55:57.120 --> 55:58.280
But, of course,

55:58.360 --> 56:03.120
not all attending tonight
will be convinced of our cause.

56:04.080 --> 56:06.000
Some will have come here tonight

56:06.080 --> 56:10.640
to find out for themselves
what we stand for.

56:10.720 --> 56:12.280
Whenever you're ready, Tom.

56:13.520 --> 56:16.040
So, here are our guiding principles:

56:16.920 --> 56:20.080
Every citizen shall serve the state.

56:20.160 --> 56:23.680
-[audience cheers and applauds]
-Not the banks, not factions.

56:24.240 --> 56:26.000
Not the Jews!

56:26.080 --> 56:30.120
[audience] Perish Judah!
Perish Judah! Perish Judah!

56:33.400 --> 56:38.840
The barriers of class will be abolished,
and a greater Britain will be born

56:38.920 --> 56:42.400
of the National Socialist
and fascist creed.

56:53.960 --> 56:56.160
It is useless to hide from ourselves

56:56.240 --> 57:01.320
the fact that ever since 1918,
when our heroes returned from France,

57:01.400 --> 57:06.240
our empire has shown
all the signs of disintegration.

57:06.320 --> 57:10.680
And our people are threatened
by gathering disaster.

57:22.720 --> 57:23.800
[indistinct shouting]

57:36.120 --> 57:36.960
[sighs]

57:37.880 --> 57:38.800
Go. Go.

57:55.760 --> 57:56.600
[watch ticking]

58:00.200 --> 58:03.640
Ten… nine…

58:06.040 --> 58:07.120
eight…

58:09.280 --> 58:10.480
seven…

58:12.920 --> 58:14.040
six…

58:16.520 --> 58:17.760
five…

58:19.520 --> 58:20.640
four…

58:21.760 --> 58:22.960
three…

58:23.040 --> 58:24.320
Two apple crumble…

58:50.640 --> 58:51.640
[muffled struggling]

59:00.360 --> 59:01.200
[grunting]

59:21.320 --> 59:23.080
[Mosley speaking indistinctly]

59:30.200 --> 59:31.600
[grunting]

59:37.840 --> 59:40.680
I think it's about time
we got off the stage, old man.

59:40.760 --> 59:42.120
Until this thing is sorted.

59:50.360 --> 59:52.760
The coppers are here.
You gotta get away from the body.

59:52.840 --> 59:53.680
[grunts]

01:00:11.360 --> 01:00:12.200
[gun cocking]

01:00:17.160 --> 01:00:18.520
What the fuck are you doing here?

01:00:18.600 --> 01:00:19.760
What happened?

01:00:19.840 --> 01:00:22.720
I don't know what happened.
I don't know what fucking happened.

01:00:22.800 --> 01:00:24.280
Doesn't make any fucking sense.

01:00:25.320 --> 01:00:27.040
-[Dogs] Wait, fuck!
-It's us.

01:00:28.120 --> 01:00:28.960
[breathing heavily]

01:00:29.040 --> 01:00:30.200
Aberama's dead.

01:00:30.680 --> 01:00:34.000
He's gone. He's gone,
and they came for me, too.

01:00:35.280 --> 01:00:37.840
What the fuck is she doing here? Huh?

01:00:37.920 --> 01:00:41.120
They got to Barney.
They knew everything.

01:00:41.200 --> 01:00:42.880
They knew fucking everything.

01:00:42.960 --> 01:00:43.800
Who?

01:00:44.640 --> 01:00:46.840
-Who knew, Tommy?
-Johnny, get this woman out of here.

01:00:46.920 --> 01:00:48.440
-I want to know.
-Get her out of here.

01:00:48.520 --> 01:00:50.040
-Come on.
-Get her out.

01:00:50.640 --> 01:00:51.480
[door opens]

01:00:52.600 --> 01:00:53.440
[door closes]

01:00:57.640 --> 01:00:58.920
Doesn't make sense.

01:01:00.920 --> 01:01:02.480
Doesn't make fucking sense.

01:01:03.400 --> 01:01:06.320
Who? Who? Who, the Chinese?

01:01:06.960 --> 01:01:08.080
The Italians?

01:01:10.280 --> 01:01:11.720
Branch.

01:01:11.800 --> 01:01:12.880
Intelligence.

01:01:12.960 --> 01:01:13.960
McCavern. Mosley.

01:01:14.040 --> 01:01:16.640
Mosley knew nothing!

01:01:16.720 --> 01:01:18.440
He knew nothing!

01:01:23.360 --> 01:01:25.320
Who?

01:01:25.400 --> 01:01:27.440
Jesus fucking Christ.

01:01:27.520 --> 01:01:29.320
You're fucking frightening me, Tom.

01:01:29.840 --> 01:01:31.040
Doesn't make sense.

01:01:34.920 --> 01:01:35.800
Who?

01:01:36.800 --> 01:01:37.680
Who?

01:01:38.560 --> 01:01:39.440
Who?

01:01:40.480 --> 01:01:42.240
-Who?
-Who?

01:01:42.320 --> 01:01:44.080
You know, Tom, you must know.

01:01:45.640 --> 01:01:48.000
You're… You're fucking scaring me.
What're you doing?

01:01:52.120 --> 01:01:53.280
[Arthur] Talk to me.

01:01:54.240 --> 01:01:55.720
[Tommy] Maybe I found him.

01:01:57.000 --> 01:01:59.040
Arthur, the man I can't defeat.

01:02:02.760 --> 01:02:04.400
-Mosley?
-I don't know.

01:02:04.480 --> 01:02:05.800
I don't fucking know.

01:02:07.600 --> 01:02:08.800
It doesn't make sense.

01:02:14.360 --> 01:02:17.120
Let's… let's go inside.

01:02:19.040 --> 01:02:20.120
We'll work it out.

01:02:20.200 --> 01:02:21.040
[sighs]

01:02:21.560 --> 01:02:23.360
-Have a drink.
-I need to walk.

01:03:07.320 --> 01:03:10.560
The work's all done, Tommy. It's all done.

01:03:11.200 --> 01:03:13.320
We can walk away from all of this.

01:03:14.560 --> 01:03:17.160
It's so easy. It's so soft.

01:03:18.240 --> 01:03:20.080
Such a small change.

01:03:22.400 --> 01:03:23.240
[screams]

01:03:25.280 --> 01:03:28.440
♪ Oh, show ♪

01:03:29.960 --> 01:03:32.760
♪ Tell me I'm the only one ♪

01:03:33.840 --> 01:03:36.760
♪ Yeah, yeah ♪

01:03:37.840 --> 01:03:41.760
♪ Like I didn't know ♪

01:03:42.800 --> 01:03:45.960
♪ Oh, show ♪

01:03:47.280 --> 01:03:50.440
♪ Tell me you're the one I can call ♪

01:03:51.040 --> 01:03:56.240
♪ Even if you choke ♪

01:04:00.200 --> 01:04:02.480
♪ Pacify, pacify ♪
